{"reference":"1 Chronicles 15","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":15,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"A reordered procession","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"After the earlier failed attempt to move the ark, David assigns the priests and Levites their proper role in carrying it. The chapter presents the new procession as deliberately ordered: the ark is carried on shoulders with its poles, while singers, musicians, gatekeepers, and priests take appointed parts in the celebration. This order frames the arrival of the ark in Jerusalem and the worship that continues before it.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 15:1-29"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_015_d996d52f1633a771e2d101d3"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}